      "confidence": "low",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "summary": "Best-effort file delete try/catch(_) idiom is copied inline across many services without a shared helper",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "ai_generated_debt",
        "related_files": [
          "lib/services/platform_bridge.dart",
          "lib/services/backup_service.dart",
          "lib/services/metadata_cover_resources.dart",
          "lib/services/replaygain_service.dart",
          "lib/services/metadata_persistence_service.dart",
          "lib/services/embedded_cover_resolver.dart"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "backup_service.dart has the pattern `try { if (await x.exists()) await x.delete(...); } catch (_) {}` at lines 95-98, 262-267, 378-381 and 497-499.",
          "metadata_cover_resources.dart 63-66, replaygain_service.dart 232-235, metadata_persistence_service.dart 135-138 and platform_bridge.dart 65-73 repeat the same shape.",
          "embedded_cover_resolver.dart already defines a private _deleteFileIfPresent helper (line 979) and still inlines the same try/catch at 785-788 and 975-976, so the helper is not shared even within one file."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Introduce one shared best-effort delete helper (for example in a small io utility) that takes a FileSystemEntity and optional recursive flag, and replace the inline copies. Keep the catches; they are intentional cleanup boundaries, but the repetition is avoidable.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "6eacebc8"
      },
